  "verbalization": "Tenalisib is implicated in targeting the DNMT3A2/3L complex through a multi-step pathway involving the Asialoglycoprotein receptor 2. The evidence suggests that Tenalisib acts as a target for the Asialoglycoprotein receptor 2, which in turn is a target of a complex compound, (1S,2R,4R)-2-bromo-1-methyl-4-[3-[(1S,2R,3S,5S)-5-methyl-3-prop-1-en-2-yl-6-oxabicyclo[3.1.1]heptan-2-yl]prop-1-en-2-yl]cyclohexan-1-ol. This compound is ultimately linked to the DNMT3A2/3L complex, indicating a potential mechanism where Tenalisib indirectly influences the DNMT3A2/3L complex through the activation of this intermediate molecule. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Tenalisib in modulating DNMT3A2/3L activity, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
